= The Curse of Shadowfen

Deep within the mist-shrouded valleys of the Northern Reach lies the forgotten township of Shadowfen. Once a thriving trading post, it now stands as a haunting reminder of prosperity lost to an ancient curse. As adventurers drawn to this forlorn place, you will uncover secrets long buried and face horrors that lurk in the perpetual twilight. #footnote[All of the content on this page was generated by AI, purely for illustrative purposes.]

#columns(2)[

  == Shadows abound

  First, gather your party at the Twisted Root Inn, where the suspicious locals eye newcomers with a mixture of hope and distrust. Rumors can be gathered here, along with potential allies and enemies disguised as friends.

  === The Festival

  Your party arrives as the autumn festival approaches—a desperate celebration meant to ward off the encroaching darkness. The town mayor, Elenora Grimshaw, has offered a substantial reward to any who can break the curse before winter's first frost. Local legends tell of a hidden temple beneath the ancient willow grove where answers might be found, but none who've sought it have returned.

